    [Feature] Enable SFA-only DSA CP for GLM-5.3 Flash (#17987)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Enable GLM-5.3 Flash SFA-only DSA CP within the TP group. Shard queries
    with full attention heads, replicate main KV/pool/tail caches, and use
    local query metadata for TopK and NoPE attention. Gather raw K/gates
    before pool compression to preserve windows crossing rank boundaries.
    KDA retains its existing TP path.
    
    Refs #15665.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Enable experimental SFA-only DSA CP with `--additional-config
    '{"enable_dsa_cp":true}'`. Use model runner V1 and keep PCP/DCP sizes at
    1.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Manual validation on 168 used `fa54d105d`, A3/CANN 9.2.0, GLM-5.3 Flash
    W8A8, TP16 + EP + FlashComm1, and FULL_DECODE_ONLY graphs.
    
    - Focused UT: **445 passed, 4 skipped**. Two-NPU checks matched
    KV/pool/tail caches and TopK exactly; attention matched at
    `atol=rtol=0.01`.
    - Full-model API checks: **20/20 passed**, including concurrent and
    image requests. MTP with 3 speculative tokens also passed **20/20**
    functional checks.
    - `vllm bench serve`: DSACP on/off end-to-end output throughput changed
    **+7.25%** (1K input, concurrency 1), **-6.89%** (1K, concurrency 16),
    and **+38.74%** (8K, concurrency 16). Fixed 128-token outputs; one
    measured run per case.
    - EvalScope 1.12.0, full GSM8K test set, 4-shot CoT, temperature 0: off
    **1284/1319 (97.35%)**, on **1281/1319 (97.12%)**, **-0.23 percentage
    points**. MTP was disabled for performance/accuracy comparisons.
    
    Runtime validation used updated host operator libraries with the fixed
    image's device binaries; a full native build failed on unrelated
    targets. Commands and raw results are preserved at
    `/root/pr17987-dsacp-20261008/workspace/`.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
